# Security review rules SEC01–SEC12

This English reference follows the security design supplement 0.1, dated 2026-10-08. The [Chinese export](../安全专项/安全自检规则.md) and its [provenance](../安全专项/安全自检规则.provenance.json) preserve the original wording and hashes. The design rules apply to a specific project's current security design or actual trial. Use the [Security SOP](security-sop.md) and the security design template for the document locale. [English template](../../assets/security-design-template.en-us.md) and [Simplified Chinese template](../安全专项/安全设计模板.md)

## 1. Review basis

Pin the project, effective requirements and decisions, objects and their own versions, platform, build, configuration, source snapshot, rule version, scope, and required evidence levels. Resolve unknown permissions before dependent action. Keep missing materials, unavailable environments, incomplete implementation, and unexecuted checks at their actual status. Record inapplicability only for capabilities absent from the applicable scope, with a reason.

For each rule, actual object, and required level, record satisfied, unsatisfied, unchecked, or inapplicable with reason. Preserve evidence and exact locations. L1 checks structure, L2 checks meaning, and L3 uses actual trials. Identify the model and tools for model-assisted review. Record design satisfaction, runtime observation, user confirmation, and residual-risk acceptance separately.

Use `CUSTOM:SEC01` through `CUSTOM:SEC12` in `sop-module-handoff-0.2` `checks.rule_id`. Use CTRL-* for actual controls. Bind `object_revision` to the actual source, interface, control, or other object version. Declare the object or record its absence as an explicit gap. A CUSTOM identifier supports structural validation. Security meaning still requires the appropriate evidence.

